   "text": {
    "L1": "We can test a food for starch, fat, and protein.",
    "L2": "A food can contain more than one nutrient, so we use separate tests.",
    "L3": "For starch, the teacher adds dilute iodine. Blue-black shows that starch is present.",
    "L4": "For fat, rub the food on paper and let it dry. An oily, translucent patch that stays shows fat.",
    "L5": "For protein, the teacher uses copper sulphate and sodium hydroxide solutions. Violet shows protein.",
    "L6": "For example, potato has starch, while groundnut has both fat and protein. Never eat tested food, and handle chemicals only with the teacher."
   },
